{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Ordinarily, no.** A retail holder of an Irish UCITS ETF sells on the exchange; only an authorised participant (AP) or other eligible institutional investor typically creates or redeems units directly with the fund, in large creation-unit blocks.\n\n**Exception:** Under the Central Bank of Ireland’s UCITS ETF rules, a secondary-market investor may redeem directly with the fund when the investor cannot redeem through the secondary market—for example, because the ETF is delisted or exchange trading is disrupted. The investor should be notified that direct redemption is available and how to exercise it.\n\nThe fund must provide a process enabling that redemption, on a timely basis and at a value reflecting the ETF’s net asset value. Any redemption charge must be limited to the cost of disinvesting the underlying assets; it must not be set so high as to deter redemption. These protections do not make direct fund redemption an ordinary alternative to exchange selling: the exceptional route applies only when secondary-market redemption is unavailable."}}
